# ⛔ THIS BOX HAS `core.autocrlf=true` AND THIS REPO HAD NO ATTRIBUTES FILE, so
# git decided text-vs-binary by SNIFFING every blob. A font that ever sniffed as
# text would have every 0x0A rewritten to 0x0D 0x0A on checkout — a corrupt
# .woff2 that @font-face rejects SILENTLY, leaving the chart axis in a fallback
# face. That is the exact failure self-hosting the font was adopted to remove, so
# it is not left to a heuristic.
#
# (Sniffing does get it right today — `git diff --cached --numstat` reports `- -`
# for all four and the stored blobs are byte-identical to disk. This is here so
# that stays true for a font whose first 8 kB happens to contain no NUL.)
#
# The self-consistency rail is in tests/test_chart_parity_harness.py: a woff2
# header declares its own total length, and CRLF conversion breaks that equality.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# note-connectors cross-language schema rail (Task 5): the Python drift test
# (`test_note_convert_fixtures.py`) byte-compares a freshly regenerated copy
# of these fixtures against the committed ones. `fixtures_gen.py` always
# writes `\n`-only. Without `eol=lf` here, `core.autocrlf=true` (this box) on
# a future clone/checkout would silently rewrite the committed copies to
# CRLF, and the drift test would then report every fixture as "stale" for a
# line-ending reason that has nothing to do with converter drift — the same
# CRLF-only-on-Windows failure class as the chart-parity harness above.
api/services/journal_two/note_connectors/convert/fixtures_in/*.md text eol=lf
api/services/journal_two/note_connectors/convert/fixtures_in/*.html text eol=lf
app/src/pages/journal-2-0/lib/importer/__fixtures__/server_convert/*.json text eol=lf

# ⛔⛔ WAVE P5 — THE FROZEN OCR CERTIFICATION CORPUS IS BYTES, NOT TEXT.
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the dev box and git guessed "text" for the one
# small mostly-ASCII fixture (`native_text.pdf`, 2.3 KB), which would rewrite
# its line endings on the next checkout and quietly change the pages the
# 5.3.0-vs-5.4.0 certification compares. The signature check would catch it —
# after somebody spent a CI run finding out.
tools/wave_p_cert_corpus/*.pdf binary
tools/wave_p_cert_corpus/manifest.json -text

# ⛔⛔ BLOBS ALREADY STORED WITH CR — `-text` SO NOTHING EVER FLATTENS THEM.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on this box, and these ten paths are committed with CRLF (one
# is MIXED). Nothing in git protects them: `git check-attr text` reported
# `unspecified` for every one, so text-vs-binary is decided by sniffing, and any tool
# that rewrites such a file "helpfully" as LF flattens the stored endings. The damage
# is not corruption — it is that a two-line edit returns as a whole-file diff and
# stops being reviewable. Measured twice in this repo (rule R-2: a 2-line edit that
# came back as 918 lines, and a 7-line edit that came back as 1,199).
#
# ⛔ `-text`, NOT `binary`. `binary` also suppresses diffs, which is a worse cure for
# a document people review — `docs/plans/joystick/deferred.md` is in this list.
#
# ⛔ THE LIST IS DERIVED, NEVER TYPED. It is every tracked path where all three hold:
# the INDEX blob contains a CR (`git grep --cached -P '\r'` — the working tree is not
# evidence, autocrlf has already put CRLF on everything there), the blob has no NUL
# (a NUL makes it binary to git already, and eol conversion never touches it), and
# `git check-attr text` says `unspecified`. Regenerate with
# `tests/test_gitattributes_eol.py::test_the_declared_list_is_still_the_derived_list`,
# which FAILS if a new such path appears — that is the rail, not this comment.
#
# ⚠️ These files belong to other programmes (charts, joystick, flow fixtures, the RTH
# scripts). This entry changes no content and no checkout bytes: a blob stored with
# CRLF already checks out as CRLF. It only removes the heuristic.
app/public/Darkpool-data.csv -text
app/public/Indexes-data.csv -text
app/public/OptionsFlow.csv -text
app/public/flow-data.csv -text
app/src/components/chart/ChartSettingsModal.chartData.test.jsx -text
app/src/components/chart/chartDataMap.js -text
app/src/components/chart/chartDataMap.test.js -text
app/src/hub/sections/homeSection.js -text
docs/plans/joystick/deferred.md -text
scripts/rth-close.ps1 -text
